            <ArticleTitle>Application of virtual three-dimensional surgery planning in management of open bite with idiopathic condylar resorption.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>249-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2231-0746.175760</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes the successful treatment of an adult patient with idiopathic condylar resorption and Class II skeletal open bite malocclusion and temporomandibular joint disorder. A segmental Le Fort I bilateral osteotomy, ramus increasing length inverted L-osteotomy, and genioplasty combined with orthodontic treatment were performed. The treatment plan and surgery was aided by three-dimensional medical modeling, and we managed to resolve functional, esthetic, and pain concerns to a satisfactory level.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
